# No internal IDs in the UI

Never expose internal database IDs (numeric or opaque FKs) to end users. Resolve every foreign key to its **business representation** before rendering.

Numeric IDs are backend implementation details. They may appear only in dedicated developer/admin debugging interfaces (explicitly labeled as such).

## Architecture (mandatory)

Enrich IPC list/get DTOs on the **backend** with display fields (`*_label`, `*_code`, `*_display_name`) via JOINs — same pattern as WO `asset_label` / `responsible_username`.

- Frontend is **presentation-only**: use enriched fields + [`src/lib/display`](src/lib/display) formatters.
- Do **not** add per-component `getById` / N+1 lookups to paint labels.
- Keep FKs on the DTO for permissions and mutations; never render them.

## Required resolution

| Stored field | Show instead |
|--------------|--------------|
| `person_id` / `user_id` / `submitter_id` | Full name (+ optional role) |
| `asset_id` / `equipment_id` | Asset code + asset name |
| `org_node_id` | Organization path (or node code + name) |
| `work_order_id` / `converted_to_wo_id` | WO code (e.g. `OT-0042`) |
| DI `id` | DI code (e.g. `DI-0007`) |
| Reference FK / code | Reference **label** (via catalog / `ReferenceCombobox` patterns) |

## Hard rules

- Do not render `#123`, `id=45`, or bare numeric FKs in lists, cards, detail panes, print, or approvals.
- If the label cannot be resolved yet, show a neutral placeholder (`—` / i18n empty) — not the raw id.
- Codes that are **business identifiers** (`DI-0001`, `EQ-PMP-01`) are allowed; surrogate keys are not.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<span>#{di.asset_id}</span>
<span>{di.submitter_id}</span>

// ✅ GOOD
<span>{formatAssetLabel(di.asset_code, di.asset_label)}</span>
<span>{formatPersonLabel(di.submitter_display_name)}</span>
```
